1. Network Details
Architecture Overview
Initial Approach – Multi-Modal MobileNetV2:
 Processed 224x224 RGB images through MobileNetV2 and 68 facial landmarks through dense layers. Features were combined and fed into two heads: an 8-class expression classifier and a valence/arousal regressor.
Final Approach – ResNet50 Multi-Task:
 Used ResNet50 backbone with global average pooling, batch normalization, and a shared dense layer before splitting into three independent branches: expression classification, valence regression, and arousal regression.
Training Configuration
Batch Size: 32


Image Size: 224x224


Optimizer: Adam with adaptive learning rates


Dataset Split: 70/30 train-test


MobileNetV2: Two-phase training (frozen backbone warmup + fine-tuning) with weighted losses favoring expression classification.
ResNet50: Progressive 30+70 epoch training, learning rate scheduling, early stopping, and model checkpointing.
Rationale for Architecture Selection
MobileNetV2: Efficient and mobile-ready, landmark fusion innovative but complex.


ResNet50: Deeper architecture, skip connections, better feature extraction, separate branches allowed task-specific optimization.



2. Multiple Baselines Comparison
Experimental Progression
MobileNetV2 Baseline: Multi-modal fusion, 29% accuracy.


Data Augmentation: Flipping, rotation, zoom, translation; 31% accuracy.


Weighted Loss: Prioritized expression classification; ~31% accuracy.


ResNet Experiments: Short ResNet50 (22%) and ResNet18 (18%) training with limited epochs.


Comprehensive ResNet50: Separate task branches, extended training, regularization; 42% accuracy.


Key Technical Improvements
Removed landmark dependency


Separate regression branches


Advanced regularization and extended training with callbacks



3. Transfer Learning Details
Strategy:
 Both architectures leveraged ImageNet pre-trained weights. Two-phase training (frozen backbone → fine-tuning) preserved learned features and accelerated convergence.
Advanced Features:
Learning rate scheduling with plateau detection


Early stopping with restoration of best weights


Memory management and checkpointing for hardware-constrained optimization

Each Time a model improved it was saved and each epoch was logged in a csv


Effectiveness:
 Transfer learning significantly improved convergence speed, feature quality, and generalization, contributing to the final 42% accuracy.

