5. Performance Measures
Evaluation Metrics:
Classification: Accuracy, F1-score, Cohen’s Kappa, Krippendorff’s Alpha, multiclass AUC


Regression: RMSE, Pearson correlation, Sign Agreement Ratio (SAGR), Concordance Correlation Coefficient (CCC)


Metric Analysis:
RMSE: Measures magnitude of error


Pearson Correlation: Measures linear relationship


SAGR: Evaluates polarity agreement for affect


CCC: Combines correlation and bias correction; gold standard for clinical validation


Results Summary:
MobileNetV2: 29% accuracy


Augmented MobileNetV2: 31% accuracy


ResNet50: 42% accuracy, used early stopping but had to manually stop at 42 epochs as my session crashes on colab due to RAM 


Balanced classification and regression performance across tasks



6. Correctly and Incorrectly Classified Images
Prediction Analysis:
Correct predictions align with valence/arousal values consistent with the classified emotion


Common failure modes include ambiguous expressions, multi-task conflicts, poor lighting, and occlusions


Multi-Task Success Criteria:
Complete success: correct expression + accurate valence/arousal


Partial success: correct in one domain only


Failures: mismatched expression or continuous predictions


Visualization:
 Generated comprehensive dashboards for confusion matrices, per-class accuracy, valence/arousal scatter plots, and residual analysis. High-confidence successes mostly occurred in clearly expressed emotions like Happy, Sad, and Neutral.

Technical Implementation Summary
Dataset and Preprocessing:
 Annotations included expressions, valence, arousal, and landmarks. Robust loading handled missing or irregular files.
Hardware Management:
GPU memory growth enabled


Batch size optimized for memory


Checkpointing for recovery from interruptions


Architecture and Modularity:
Centralized configuration for reproducibility


Fixed seeds for deterministic results


Advanced Training Features:
Learning rate scheduling, early stopping


Two-phase progressive training


Comprehensive callbacks for monitoring


Evaluation Framework:
Multi-task metrics with automated calculation


Visualization for training history and prediction analysis


Key Achievements:
Multi-modal integration initially explored


Advanced ResNet50 architecture with task-specific branches


Transfer learning and fine-tuning optimized within hardware limits


Specialized metrics (SAGR, CCC) used for comprehensive assessment


Lessons Learned:
ResNet50 superior to MobileNetV2 for complex facial affect recognition


Progressive transfer learning more effective than single-stage training


Metric selection and visualization critical for model understanding


Hardware-aware training strategies essential


Final Outcome:
 Systematic improvements raised performance from 29% to 42% accuracy, demonstrating effective deep learning engineering and multi-task optimization.


